# ==============================================================================
# Project Forge .gitignore
# ==============================================================================

# ----- Environment & Secrets -----
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.cert
credentials.json
secrets.json

# ----- Claude / AI Tooling -----
# Ignore .claude contents by default, then whitelist essentials
.claude/*
# Track project config, taskboard, skills, hooks, rules, agents
!.claude/CLAUDE.md
!.claude/rules/
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/agents/
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/tools/
!.claude/workflows/
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/TASKBOARD_SETUP.md
!.claude/SANDBOX.md
!.claude/docs/
# Always ignore local settings, DB, and WAL files
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/taskboard.db
.claude/taskboard.db-wal
.claude/taskboard.db-shm
# Generated sync state — not for version control
.claude/hooks/github-project-map.json
.claude/hooks/.sync-push.lock
.claude/hooks/.sync-lock-wanted
.claude/hooks/.sync-disabled
.claude/hooks/.sync.log

# ----- Windsurf / AI Tooling -----
# Track Windsurf rules and workflows
!.windsurf/
!.windsurf/rules/
!.windsurf/workflows/
specs/
ARCHITECTURE.md
project_board.json

# ----- Rust / Cargo -----
engine/target/
.transform-gizmo-fork/target/
engine/pkg/
engine/pkg-webgl2/
engine/pkg-webgpu/
engine/pkg-webgl2-runtime/
engine/pkg-webgpu-runtime/

# ----- WASM Build Artifacts (intermediate) -----
# WASM engine binaries are hosted on CDN (Cloudflare R2), not committed to git.
# Set NEXT_PUBLIC_ENGINE_CDN_URL in production to point to the CDN origin.
web/public/engine-pkg-webgl2/
web/public/engine-pkg-webgpu/
web/public/engine-pkg-webgl2-runtime/
web/public/engine-pkg-webgpu-runtime/

# ----- Node / npm -----
# Bare (no trailing slash) on purpose: worktrees symlink web/node_modules at the
# main repo's tree, and a `node_modules/` pattern matches only real directories.
node_modules
web/package-lock.json
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# ----- Next.js -----
web/.next/
web/out/
web/test-results/
web/auth-results/
web/playwright-report/
web/playwright-report-crossbrowser/
web/blob-report/
# Playwright MCP browser-session scratch output (console-*.log / page-*.yml)
.playwright-mcp/

# ----- Coverage -----
coverage/

# ----- Packages -----
packages/ui/dist/

# ----- TypeScript -----
*.tsbuildinfo

# ----- OS Files -----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
ehthumbs.db
ehthumbs_vista.db
nul

# ----- IDE / Editor -----
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.project
.settings/
.classpath

# ----- Session artifacts -----
PHASE-*.md
REFACTOR*.md
# ...but not the vendored tdd skill's refactoring.md (case-insensitive FS makes
# REFACTOR*.md swallow it, leaving its SKILL.md link dangling on a fresh checkout).
!.agents/skills/tdd/refactoring.md
*-SUMMARY.md
*-PROGRESS.md
rust_errors.txt
*.backup
do_split.py
extract_handlers.py
split_commands*.py

# ----- AutoForge -----
autoforge/results/*
!autoforge/results/.gitkeep
autoforge/asset-cache/*
!autoforge/asset-cache/.gitkeep
autoforge/node_modules/

# ----- Misc -----
*.log
*.pid
*.seed
*.pid.lock
.cache/
.claude/hooks/__pycache__/

# Taskboard DB files — use OS default path, never commit
.claude/taskboard.db
.claude/taskboard.db-shm
.claude/taskboard.db-wal

# Generated MCP command pages (regenerated on every build)
apps/docs/content/mcp/*.mdx
.vercel
.claude/.env-health-last-check
.worktrees/

# --- Machine artefacts that must never be committed (#9736 follow-up) ---
# A literal `%SystemDrive%` directory appeared at the repo root: a Windows
# environment variable written into a path by a tool running under a POSIX
# shell, which does not expand it. It contained copies of Windows cache
# databases. Ignored so a recurrence cannot be swept in by `git add -A`, and
# named here so the next person to see one knows what it is.
# ANCHORED TO THE REPO ROOT. Unanchored, git matches these at EVERY depth —
# verified with `git check-ignore -v`, which reported a nested
# `web/src/%USERPROFILE%/deep/file.txt` as ignored by this rule (found in
# review). Nobody creates such a directory on purpose, so the practical risk is
# small, but the incident this guards against happened at the root: a tool run
# from the repo root wrote an unexpanded environment variable as a path.
#
# The narrower rule also fails in the safer direction. A tool run from a
# SUBDIRECTORY now creates its `%VAR%` directory somewhere these patterns do not
# cover, where it shows up in `git status` as an untracked oddity rather than
# being silently ignored — visible is better than hidden for something that
# should not exist at all.
/%SystemDrive%/
/%USERPROFILE%/
/%LOCALAPPDATA%/

# --- Codex CLI surface (#9745) -------------------------------------------------
# `.codex/agents/*.toml`, `.codex/hooks.json` and the project skills under
# `.agents/skills/` are GENERATED from `.claude/` by tools/agentic-sync/port.mjs
# and are tracked; scripts/check-codex-port.sh fails a PR on any drift. They were
# ignored here while a hand-copied port was unfinished (143 dead `.Codex/...`
# references, 26 of 39 hooks wired); that quarantine is lifted by the change that
# replaced the copies with the generator.
#
# `.codex/hooks/` holds ONE tracked file, the adapter that runs the shared
# `.claude/hooks/*.sh` scripts under Codex. Everything else in it stays ignored:
# the first port copied all of `.claude/hooks/` there, including a log, two lock
# files, a `__pycache__` and a 400 KB `.bak`, and a checkout that still carries
# those copies must not have them swept in by a `git add -A`. The scripts are
# NOT duplicated any more — a second copy is a second thing to keep patched, and
# three of the old copies had already fallen behind their originals (#9955).
.codex/hooks/*
!.codex/hooks/run-claude-hook.mjs
